\begin{assum}[Ellipsoid Action Set] \label{assum:ellipsoid} We assume $\mathcal A_{n, t} = \gA_t = \{x^\top \mQ_t^{-1} x \le 1: x \in \mathbb R^d\}$ is an ellipsoid with $\lambda_{\min}(\mQ_t) \ge \lambda_0 = \Omega(1)$. 
\end{assum}
The first assumption states that each action set is an ellipsoid that covers all directions.
This is a standard assumption, e.g., see \cite{rusmevichientong2010linearly}.

In this setting, we will also need to put some additional assumptions on the underlying parameters $\mB$ and $\mW$.
% [printed: Assumption 4]
\begin{assum}[Diverse Source Tasks] We assume that $\lambda_{\min}(\frac{1}{T}\mW \mW^\top) \ge \frac{\nu}{k}$, where $\nu = \Omega(1)$. \label{assum:diverse}
\end{assum}
